<h1>ON-LANGAGE - Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>Last updated: November 15, 2026</p>

<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>ON-LANGAGE is a language-learning application offering lessons, vocabulary, examinations and educational certificates.</p>

<h2>2. Information You Provide</h2>
<p>The application may ask for your first name, last name and identification number (ID/RUT) to prepare educational certificates and diplomas.</p>

<h2>3. Learning Progress</h2>
<p>ON-LANGAGE may store your course progress, examination results and certificate preferences locally on your device.</p>

<h2>4. Internet Access</h2>
<p>Some features, including online translation, may require an internet connection. Text submitted for translation may be processed by an external translation service.</p>

<h2>5. Advertising</h2>
<p>ON-LANGAGE may display advertisements through Google AdMob. Advertising services may collect or process device identifiers and other information according to their own privacy policies.</p>
<p>Google Privacy Policy:
<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a></p>

<h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>
<p>Information may be processed by third-party services necessary for translation and advertising. ON-LANGAGE does not sell personal information directly.</p>

<h2>7. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
<p>Locally stored learning information may be removed by clearing the application's data or uninstalling the application. Information processed by external services is subject to their respective policies.</p>

<h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>ON-LANGAGE is an educational application. Parents and guardians should supervise children's use of online translation and advertising features.</p>

<h2>9. Security</h2>
<p>We aim to protect user information, but no electronic storage or internet transmission method is completely secure.</p>

<h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>This policy may be updated when the application's features or data practices change.</p>

<h2>11. Contact</h2>
<p>For privacy questions, contact the ON-LANGAGE developer through the contact information published on the application's Google Play listing.</p>
